{"family": "parseq", "task": "ocr", "name": "PARSeq (scene text recognition)", "plain": "PARSeq (Bautista and Atienza, ECCV 2022): reads one cropped word (Latin letters, digits, punctuation) with a Vision Transformer and a small decoder that refines its own guess; a base and a tiny version. Apache-2.0 code and weights.", "summary": "PARSeq (Bautista and Atienza, ECCV 2022): a ViT encoder over the word crop (32 x 128) and one two-stream Transformer decoder layer trained with permuted autoregressive sequence modelling; reads one cropped word or short line (94 characters: Latin letters, digits, ASCII punctuation; no space). Greedy autoregressive decoding plus one refinement pass, as upstream `read.py`. A recogniser only: the whole input is one line (one quad over the image); pair it with a detector (e.g. `ppocrv5-mobile` boxes) for full pages.", "tier": "experimental", "upstream": "https://github.com/baudm/parseq", "upstream_commit": "1902db043c029a7e03a3818c616c06600af574be", "original_is": null, "papers": [{"title": "Scene Text Recognition with Permuted Autoregressive Sequence Models", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.06966", "date": "2022-07-14", "venue": "ECCV 2022", "variants": []}], "official": [], "modes": ["portable", "kernels"], "portable_dtype": "float16", "kernels_dtype": "float16", "kernel_libs": ["pil_resample"], "mps_kernel_libs": [], "mps_dtypes": ["float32", "float16"], "no_kernels_reason": "", "no_original_reason": "", "options": [{"name": "cuda_graphs", "default": true, "bounds": "", "effect": "speed"}], "outputs": [{"name": "boxes", "extra": false}, {"name": "texts", "extra": false}, {"name": "scores", "extra": false}], "output_info": {}, "licence_files": ["LICENSE", "NOTICE"], "licence_notes": [], "limitations": [], "task_io": "Input: one RGB image. Output: the text lines in reading order: a quad `[N, 4, 2]` per line, its text and a confidence `[N]` (text detector + recogniser; recognisers alone read the whole image as one line).", "install": {"ex